WEBVTT

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.440
Could you tell me what room
Colonel Roy Mustang is staying in?

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.190
Let's see...

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.450
May I have your name, please?

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.110
The name's Nox. Doctor in private practice.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.370
He'll know right away.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.390
Final Episode

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.390
Final Episode

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.390
Journey's End

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.390
Journey's End

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.370
Hey, princess.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.790
It's been a while.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.050
Who might that be?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.260
I need him here for a reason.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.760
He's what I'd call my trump card.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.520
So, is he down in the dumps?

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.770
The main method of cultivation in the Ishbal area is double-cropping,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.650
Bzzzt, try again.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.780
They raise the same crop semiannually.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.990
You expect to gain their trust like this?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:58.990
I know!

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.240
Moving on.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.910
So what crop do they raise with that method?

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.500
Barley and cotton.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.580
Correct.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.120
So you DO know your stuff.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.670
Don't underestimate me.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.340
I've been doing some research for a while.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.260
He's planning to solve the Ishbalan crisis before becoming the Führer President.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.090
"Solving"?

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.600
But first things first, "becoming the Führer President"?

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.850
Is that you, Dr. Nox?

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.810
Yo.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.360
Looks like... you're doing okay.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.570
Yeah.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.690
These guys won't leave me alone.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.030
No breaks, no nothing.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.990
Not exactly what I meant.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.570
Aren't your eyes...

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:39.820
Yeah.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.580
Apparently, it's the punishment Truth gave to someone who dreamt of the future.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.330
Are you okay?

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.710
Not sure about that.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.340
Either way, I can't stop here.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.670
Führer President...

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.090
Well, to take care of Ishbal first.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.100
The Ishbal Annihilation...

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.100
That was what started everything.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:11.020
Yup. Both for you, and for me.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.860
I'm going to set things right.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:13.860
Meaning?

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.860
First, I'm going to open up the areas in Ishbal that are currently off-limits.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.820
Then, I'm going to allow the Ishbalans living in each slums back to their Holy Land.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.120
There's much more to be done.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.500
We were able to overcome the crisis
thanks to Scar and the other people of Ishbal.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.290
We're in their debt, after all.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.050
Colonel, I brought the data you asked for.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.550
It's not as if our sins will be forgiven,
but we want to start with what we can.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.180
Christ, you lot...

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.890
Yo, it looks like they took the words out of our mouths, Dr. Marcoh.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.020
Marcoh?

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.350
Dr. Marcoh?!

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.650
Colonel Mustang.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.660
I've got a philosopher's stone right here.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.290
We should be able to get your vision back with this.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.160
You're right.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.670
I made this stone in the past by using the lives of Ishbalans.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:28.560
I have no right to say this, but if it's for the sake of reviving Ishbal, I'm sure they'll...

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:37.230
No, I cannot hear their voices.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.860
So this is a request from myself.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.700
I want to patch you up with this stone for the sake of Ishbal.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.200
They might get angry.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.750
Fullmetal, too.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.710
But I'll gladly take your offer.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.680
And with that, I'll give it my all.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.890
But before that...

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.640
...there's someone who needs the power of the stone more than I.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.020
I can come after him.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.240
Havoc General Store, happily serving for 80 years now!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.700
Oh, Breda. What's up?

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.870
What?! You want me to head down to Central NOW?!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.920
What do you mean, "you'll find out when you get there"?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.840
How are your wounds treating you, Scar?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.430
Why did you save me?

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.930
Initially to find out more about Eastern Alchemy,

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.390
but the situation has changed.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.600
Mustang wants Miles for his new Ishbal policy.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.560
And so, I decided to take you along.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.280
Not as "Scar," but as someone of the Ishbalan race.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.240
What do you say?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.870
Won't you help us in reviving the Ishbalan religion?

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.950
We cannot let a religion and a culture so rich in history die out.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.960
The death of a culture equates to the death of its people.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.960
Save the people from death with your hands.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.340
The meaning of being kept alive...

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:32.010
So you want me to live for a bit longer to find what that is, huh, Brother?

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.430
Fine.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.730
I'll help you out.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.980
Take me wherever you please.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.150
Okay, Miles. I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.860
Do things safely.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:47.610
Roger.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.860
That Mustang...

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:54.450
He'd probably be frightened to death
if he were to find out that Scar is alive.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.080
Scar.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.870
What is your true name?

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.630
I've died twice.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.260
I don't exist in this world.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.850
Thus, I don't need a name.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.010
Call me whatever you please.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.640
I see.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:20.770
We'll meet again, Ishbalan.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.410
You okay?

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.040
I didn't imagine that my muscles would be this weak.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.040
Want a ride on my back?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.800
Nah.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.550
I want to walk with my own two legs.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.970
I'll take it slow, so you go on ahead.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.970
Nah. We left the house together.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.310
We have to go back together, too.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.690
Well then, let's go.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.190
Yeah.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.740
Brother, your leg...

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:20.040
Yeah... I haven't had maintenance on it in forever.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.630
Thanks.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.500
For what?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.420
Nothing.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.710
What the heck?

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:31.260
Weirdo.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.800
Oh yeah, I wonder if Lin and the others have arrived in Xing already.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:42.190
It's been two months since then, so I'm sure they have.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.270
I hope May is okay...

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.690
Don't worry.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.280
Just leave everything to him.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.580
May...

00:07:58.370 --> 00:07:59.370
Sir Al...

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.250
What's the matter?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.750
Nothing.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.580
Hey you, the princess from the Chan clan.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:08.840
Lin Yao!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.300
Whoa, don't give me that scary look.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.050
You're such a klutz.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:22.230
In the end, you were unable to obtain a philosopher's stone because you were meddling in another country's affairs.

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:27.440
The Yao clan will now be in control.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.820
But don't fret.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:38.280
Our clan will protect yours.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:44.080
I'm the man who even accepted the Homunculus Greed.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:49.130
I'll accept the Chan clan along with all of the other clans.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.180
Just look at you.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:01.060
Don't worry. People from Xing always keep promises, right?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:05.180
You'll "accept us all"? That's so greedy, Lin Yao!

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.610
Shoot, maybe he rubbed off on me.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.860
Well, then... guess we should start heading back.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:19.160
Already?

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.160
Yeah.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.870
I want to give Fu a proper burial.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:25.870
Later.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.960
Yup, later.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.470
So many things happened...

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.840
Yeah.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.260
By the way, Alphonse.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:46.430
Seems like the princess of Xing,
May Chan, really took a liking to you.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.440
Yeah, she's such a nice girl.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:52.320
Moving right along, what about things between you and Winry?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.760
Den! It's me!

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.060
Customers...?

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.440
Den, that tickles!

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.620
Welcome home, idiots!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.080
Yo!

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.000
Good to be home!

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.880
Oww!!

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.760
2 Years Later

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.760
2 Years Later

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.390
I suck at stuff like this...

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.850
Nothing, huh...

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.120
Ah, well.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.540
Brother, you still haven't fixed it yet?

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:57.290
I'm all worn out from greeting people.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.000
Winry knows that, but she's treating me like her slave.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.460
On top of that-

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:06.300
She wants you to come down for tea
now that her apple pie is out of the oven.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:08.640
Okay.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.390
We have a pretty amazing view today!

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.390
Yeah.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.690
The world is so vast.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.060
Yup.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.530
Brother, there's something that's been on my mind for a while.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:29.030
I'm probably thinking of the same thing.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.790
How is your work?

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:41.710
There are so many things to worry about; I feel like I suddenly aged twenty years.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:49.430
But I have Mustang and Armstrong fulfilling their duties in the east and the north, respectively.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:53.680
Thanks to them, an old geezer like me can somehow manage to perform my duties as the Führer President.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.310
I really owe them a lot.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.060
Are you not going to give away your position?

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:04.480
I can't hand it over to the young ones just yet.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.940
Oh, my.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.410
You sound just like my late husband.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.200
He was always totally committed to work, like you are.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.750
Oh no, I'm the most...

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.960
...irresponsible person I know.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.170
Oh my, Selim.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.300
What's the matter?

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.090
This little birdy is hurt.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.140
Could you help him?

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.810
Oh, no.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.690
Have the butler call a veterinarian.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.520
Will... Will he get better?

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.110
Of course he will.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.980
Run along now.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.950
He's grown into such a kind boy.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.410
He has.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:57.450
Everyone protested when I decided I'd raise him,

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.540
but he's grown so much without giving me reason to worry.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.460
We're going to be keeping an eye on him for just a little while longer.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.680
You're aware what we'll have to do...

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.560
...if he causes trouble, right?

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.810
I won't let him.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:31.320
A homunculus and a human.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:35.830
Will they really be able to understand each other?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:42.500
New possibilities get you excited no matter how old you are.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.380
Is Edward not depressed about his left leg?

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.050
Not at all.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:58.100
He even said, "As punishment, I'd rather keep my leg as an automail."

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.100
I see.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.850
He also said, "Winry'll cry if I don't have this."

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.110
What in the world?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.400
I'm so glad you two got your bodies back.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.240
I'm sure Maes will be happy too.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.120
Starting with Mr. Hughes,

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:30.670
So many different people from so many different places helped us be happy.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.050
And that's why I feel like it's our turn to give back.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:38.300
Is that what you alchemists call "Equivalent Exchange"?

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:43.180
Nope. If we received 10 and gave 10 back,
everything would be the same.

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:48.310
If we receive 10, we add an extra and give back 11.

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:52.780
It's very minor, but it's a new rule my brother and I came up with.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.700
But now we're going to have to live up to our word.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.200
There's something you want to do, isn't there?

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.710
There's a girl we couldn't save.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:11.710
We still can't forget about her.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.510
Welcome!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.510
Mr. Jerso, Mr. Zampano.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.260
Yo.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.930
We've got a ton of food. Eat up.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:21.890
Okay.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:25.310
Excuse me! Can I get a glass of milk and a sandwich?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.140
Coming right up!

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:32.150
I see. So you've already paid your respects.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.480
Yup.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.070
Then it's...

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:35.650
...time.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.410
I'm going to Xing.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.950
I plan on studying Eastern Alchemy full-scale at May's place.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.410
Not just Xing.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:50.040
I want to go around all the eastern countries to study various things.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.920
I want to see and learn many things.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.760
I also want to meet many new people.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.930
But wait, are you two really coming along?

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:02.760
Of course!

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.430
Our wild instincts tell us...

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.560
...that coming along with you...

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:10.730
...will get us something great!!

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.820
Alphonse.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.780
We're going to look for a way to return to our old bodies.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.450
You're the one who told us not to give up.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.290
We have to do things ourselves
instead of having others do the work.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:27.790
Right!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:31.130
Isn't your brother coming to Xing?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.250
Nah.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:36.420
I'm taking the eastern route,
and he's taking the western route.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:40.050
And once the two of us gather the knowledge we gained from both directions,

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:43.760
we may be able to avoid the same kind of tragedy that happened to Nina.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.430
But, you know...

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.940
That's not the only reason why we're traveling.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:55.440
We want to see just how vast the world is!

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:58.610
You need to oil it every day.

00:18:58.610 --> 00:18:59.610
Sure.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.820
And check to make sure all the screws are tight.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:03.030
Sure.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:05.370
Dry it off after coming out of the shower.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.200
Sure...

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.460
Hey, are you even listening?!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:10.870
Sure...

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:11.670
Geez...

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.670
Well, here it is!

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:27.430
With this attitude, you're just going to end up
breaking it and having to come back again soon.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:30.310
Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.690
When you need maintenance,
be sure to call in for an appointment.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:35.940
Sure.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:42.320
Appointment...

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.700
What?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.210
Winry...

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:58.630
What is it? Just speak up if you've got something to say.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.390
It's equivalent exchange!

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:11.600
I'll give you half of my life, so you give me half of yours!

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.570
Oh, geez!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.200
Why do alchemists have to be like this?

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.160
"Equivalent Exchange"? Are you retarded?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.490
What did you say?!

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:32.370
You really are stupid.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.670
Half? I'll give you all of it.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.970
W-Wait, maybe not all of it!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:46.890
90 percent...

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.890
Or maybe.. 80 percent?

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.600
A bit more than 70...

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.640
Okay then, 85 percent?

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.980
Sure! I can give you that much!

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.270
W-What?!

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:58.770
Ed!

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.230
My bad, my bad.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:03.780
Ed!!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.700
You really are amazing.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:11.790
You're able to overturn the law of equivalent exchange so easily.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.910
What do you mean by that?

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.290
Are you making fun of me?

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.460
I'm not.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:23.340
That cheered me up. Thanks.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:25.260
I'll be off now.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.180
Safe trip!

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:50.200
Oh my, even Edward left on a trip?

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.450
Why don't they settle down a little?

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:55.700
For them, this is fine.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.170
Men who keep still are no fun.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.960
A lesson without pain is meaningless.

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:11.930
That's because no one can gain without sacrificing something.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:17.850
But by enduring that pain and overcoming it...

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:23.190
...he shall obtain a powerful, unmatched heart.

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:27.360
A fullmetal heart.

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:33.620
Drawn by a landscape as white as snow,

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:33.620
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:40.170
I'm headed toward an unseen world.

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:40.170
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:49.110
I've been traveling while lost

00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:49.110
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:51.900
Under this gray sky.

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:51.890
Nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:57.990
Every day with new maps, stained with my many dreams.

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:57.990
Higawari no chizu ikutsumo no yume ga nijindeita

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:00.380
I wonder if someday,

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:00.380
Itsuka wa sa

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:04.420
Even with these tiny steps of mine,

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:04.420
Chippoke na boku no kono hohaba demo

00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:10.500
I'll be able to travel beyond those clouds.

00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:10.500
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:12.130
I put on a bold front.

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:12.130
Tsuyogatte

00:23:12.130 --> 00:23:13.680
End up hurting myself.

00:23:12.130 --> 00:23:13.680
Kizutsuita

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:16.760
I feel empty inside.

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:16.760
Kokoro sukashita youni

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:18.300
It's started to rain,

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:18.300
Furidashita

00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:20.470
And the raindrops

00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:20.470
Amatsubu tachi ga

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:23.690
Began to repeat their scattered reflections.

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:23.690
Ranhansha kurikaesu

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:26.560
These straight rays of light

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:26.560
Massugu na hikari ga

00:23:26.560 --> 00:23:29.280
Start to cross one another.

00:23:26.560 --> 00:23:29.280
Kousa shite

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:32.860
And without telling anyone where they're headed,

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:32.860
Yakusaki mo tsugenumama

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:34.150
Across the endless distances,

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:34.150
Doko made mo

00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:35.740
They pass through all matter.

00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:35.740
Tsukinukeru

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:41.570
I burn these faint afterimages onto my eyes.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:41.570
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakitsukete

00:23:41.570 --> 00:23:43.490
Under this sky,

00:23:41.570 --> 00:23:43.490
Kono sora no shita

00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:47.320
Wherever I am,

00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:47.320
Donna toko ni itemo

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:49.620
I should be able to reach

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:49.620
Todoku hazu nanda

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:54.430
The unseen world.

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:54.430
Mada minu sekai e
